{"id":"DRKS00032543","src":"drks","title":"National paediatric rheumatologic database","official":"","summary":"The National Pediatric Rheumatologic Database (NPRD) has been conducted nationwide since 1997. The Gesellschaft für Kinder- und Jugendrheumatologie (GKJR) recommends participation as a quality assurance measure. As part of the documentation, children and adolescents with inflammatory rheumatic diseases who visit pediatric rheumatology centers once a year, along with their treating physicians, are asked to complete standardized doctor and patient or parent questionnaires. The physicians provide information about the diagnosis, disease activity, and treatment. From the patient and parent side, data about the health status and quality of life of the affected individuals are documented.","conditions":["Juvenile arthritis","Juvenile arthritis in psoriasis","Chronic multifocal osteomyelitis","Dermatopolymyositis","Other overlap syndromes","Systemic sclerosis","Systemic lupus erythematosus","Polyarteritis nodosa and related conditions","Other necrotizing vasculopathies","Arteritis, unspecified","autoinflammatory diseases"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"No interventions are carried out. This is purely an observational study, which is conducted once a year."}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nSigned consent form\r\n(Suspected) juvenile rheumatic disease\nExclusion criteria:\nrefusal to participate","minAge":"","maxAge":"25 Years","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":null,"start":"2007-05-01","pcd":"","upd":"2026-04-16","sponsor":"Deutsches Rheuma-Forschungszentrum (DRFZ)","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Prof. Dr. Kirsten Minden · Deutsches Rheuma-Forschungszentrum (DRFZ) · +49 (0)30 28460 669 · minden@drfz.de"],"sites":[{"f":"Helios Klinikum Berlin-Buch","city":"Berlin","zip":"","s":"R","pr":"","c":"","lat":52.5244,"lon":13.4105},{"f":"Universitätsmedizin Berlin - Charité","city":"Berlin","zip":"","s":"R","